{
  // X: Beyond the Frontier's ship roster. X-Tension has its own in games/xtension; the two
  // executables disagree on most numbers, so neither game borrows the other's.
  //
  // Each entry has two halves. Everything above "// ours" is the original game's own data, read
  // from the ship table compiled into the executable — regenerate it with
  //     dotnet run --project tools/OpenXt.AssetImport -- ships --game xbtf --json
  // Speed and acceleration are in the m/s the game displays (raw / 222, calibrated against
  // elite-games.ru's ship database; the X-Tension manual prints the raw numbers as if they were m/s).
  // Ship statistics are facts about the game, not copyrighted assets, so they live here; meshes,
  // textures and the games' text never do. Body and text ids are the table's own pairing.
  //
  // Below "// ours" is hand-authored: the game has no notion of mass, so mass, manoeuvring thrust,
  // turn rates and the collision radius are set per class and race and tuned by feel. Two flight
  // values follow the game: cruiseSpeed = speed, mainThrust = mass x acceleration.
  //
  // XBTF's table holds flight data only: class, speed, acceleration and steering. There is no
  // cargo, hull or equipment for these ships in X.exe — the code reads nothing past the
  // acceleration — so those fields are absent here rather than guessed.
  //
  // Left out on purpose: stations, the Commandship (2901), training drones (2911), the Xenon
  // Mother's tower and other "Unknown Object" props.
  //
  // A mod changes this roster by layering its own data/ships/ships.json; entries merge by id.
